{"id":"15","title":"Indefinite Integrals","subs":[{"id":"15.1","title":"Integration by Substitution","n":12},{"id":"15.2","title":"Integration by Parts","n":7},{"id":"15.3","title":"Partial Fractions, Algebraic and Special Forms","n":8}],"questions":[{"id":"A15-0001","n":1,"sub":"15.1","yr":1995,"d":"1995-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1995","type":"mcq","q":"The value of the integral \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{\\cos^3x+\\cos^5x}{\\sin^2x+\\sin^4x}dx\\) is","opts":["\\(\\sin x-6\\tan^{-1}(\\sin x)+c\\)","\\(\\sin x-2(\\sin x)^{-1}+c\\)","\\(\\sin x-2(\\sin x)^{-1}-6\\tan^{-1}(\\sin x)+c\\)","\\(\\sin x-2(\\sin x)^{-1}+5\\tan^{-1}(\\sin x)+c\\)"],"ans":2,"sol":"With \\(t=\\sin x\\): \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{(1-t^2)(2-t^2)}{t^2(1+t^2)}dt=\\int\\left(1+\\dfrac2{t^2}-\\dfrac6{1+t^2}\\right)dt=t-\\dfrac2t-6\\tan^{-1}t\\)."},{"id":"A15-0002","n":2,"sub":"15.2","yr":2000,"d":"2000-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 2000","type":"mcq","q":"Let \\(f(x)=\\displaystyle\\int e^x(x-1)(x-2)dx\\) then \\(f\\) decreases in the interval,","opts":["\\((-\\infty,-2)\\)","\\((-2,-1)\\)","\\((1,2)\\)","\\((2,\\infty)\\)"],"ans":2,"sol":"\\(f'(x)=e^x(x-1)(x-2)&lt;0\\) exactly for \\(1&lt;x&lt;2\\)."},{"id":"A15-0003","n":3,"sub":"15.3","yr":2006,"d":"2006-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 2006","type":"mcq","q":"\\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{x^2-1}{x^3\\sqrt{2x^4-2x^2+1}}dx=\\)","opts":["\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2x^4-2x^2+1}}{x^2}+c\\)","\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2x^4-2x^2+1}}{x^3}+c\\)","\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2x^4-2x^2+1}}x+c\\)","\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2x^4-2x^2+1}}{2x^2}+c\\)"],"ans":3,"sol":"Divide by \\(x^2\\) inside the root: \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{\\frac1{x^3}-\\frac1{x^5}}{\\sqrt{2-\\frac2{x^2}+\\frac1{x^4}}}dx\\). With \\(t=2-\\frac2{x^2}+\\frac1{x^4}\\), \\(dt=4\\left(\\frac1{x^3}-\\frac1{x^5}\\right)dx\\): \\(\\frac14\\cdot2\\sqrt t\\)."},{"id":"A15-0004","n":4,"sub":"15.1","yr":2007,"d":"2007-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 2007","type":"mcq","q":"Let \\(f(x)=\\dfrac x{(1+x^n)^{1/n}}\\) for \\(n\\ge2\\) and \\(g(x)=\\underbrace{(f\\,o\\,f\\,o\\ldots o\\,f)}_{f\\text{ occurs }n\\text{ times}}(x)\\). Then \\(\\displaystyle\\int x^{n-2}g(x)\\,dx\\) equals","opts":["\\(\\dfrac1{n(n-1)}(1+nx^n)^{1-\\frac1n}+K\\)","\\(\\dfrac1{n-1}(1+nx^n)^{1-\\frac1n}+K\\)","\\(\\dfrac1{n(n+1)}(1+nx^n)^{1+\\frac1n}+K\\)","\\(\\dfrac1{n+1}(1+nx^n)^{1+\\frac1n}+K\\)."],"ans":0,"sol":"\\(f(f(x))=\\dfrac x{(1+2x^n)^{1/n}}\\) and, repeating, \\(g(x)=\\dfrac x{(1+nx^n)^{1/n}}\\). With \\(u=1+nx^n\\), \\(du=n^2x^{n-1}dx\\): \\(\\dfrac1{n^2}\\displaystyle\\int u^{-1/n}du=\\dfrac{u^{1-\\frac1n}}{n(n-1)}\\)."},{"id":"A15-0005","n":5,"sub":"15.3","yr":2008,"d":"2008-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 2008","type":"mcq","q":"Let \\(I=\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{e^x}{e^{4x}+e^{2x}+1}dx\\), \\(J=\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{e^{-x}}{e^{-4x}+e^{-2x}+1}dx\\). Then, for an arbitrary constant \\(C\\), the value of \\(J-I\\) equals","opts":["\\(\\dfrac12\\log\\left(\\dfrac{e^{4x}-e^{2x}+1}{e^{4x}+e^{2x}+1}\\right)+C\\)","\\(\\dfrac12\\log\\left(\\dfrac{e^{2x}+e^x+1}{e^{2x}-e^x+1}\\right)+C\\)","\\(\\dfrac12\\log\\left(\\dfrac{e^{2x}-e^x+1}{e^{2x}+e^x+1}\\right)+C\\)","\\(\\dfrac12\\log\\left(\\dfrac{e^{4x}+e^{2x}+1}{e^{4x}-e^{2x}+1}\\right)+C\\)"],"ans":2,"sol":"With \\(u=e^x\\): \\(I=\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{du}{u^4+u^2+1}\\) and \\(J=\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{e^{3x}dx}{e^{4x}+e^{2x}+1}=\\int\\dfrac{u^2\\,du}{u^4+u^2+1}\\). So \\(J-I=\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{u^2-1}{u^4+u^2+1}du=\\int\\dfrac{1-\\frac1{u^2}}{\\left(u+\\frac1u\\right)^2-1}du=\\dfrac12\\log\\dfrac{u+\\frac1u-1}{u+\\frac1u+1}=\\dfrac12\\log\\dfrac{u^2-u+1}{u^2+u+1}\\). <i>(The book interchanges the names \\(I\\) and \\(J\\); the paper's version is used here.)</i>"},{"id":"A15-0006","n":6,"sub":"15.1","yr":2012,"d":"2012-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 2012","type":"mcq","q":"The integral \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{\\sec^2x}{(\\sec x+\\tan x)^{9/2}}dx\\) equals (for some arbitrary constant \\(K\\))","opts":["\\(-\\dfrac1{(\\sec x+\\tan x)^{11/2}}\\left\\{\\dfrac1{11}-\\dfrac17(\\sec x+\\tan x)^2\\right\\}+K\\)","\\(\\dfrac1{(\\sec x+\\tan x)^{11/2}}\\left\\{\\dfrac1{11}-\\dfrac17(\\sec x+\\tan x)^2\\right\\}+K\\)","\\(-\\dfrac1{(\\sec x+\\tan x)^{11/2}}\\left\\{\\dfrac1{11}+\\dfrac17(\\sec x+\\tan x)^2\\right\\}+K\\)","\\(\\dfrac1{(\\sec x+\\tan x)^{11/2}}\\left\\{\\dfrac1{11}+\\dfrac17(\\sec x+\\tan x)^2\\right\\}+K\\)"],"ans":2,"sol":"With \\(t=\\sec x+\\tan x\\): \\(\\sec x=\\frac12\\left(t+\\frac1t\\right)\\) and \\(dt=t\\sec x\\,dx\\). The integral is \\(\\dfrac12\\displaystyle\\int\\left(t^{-9/2}+t^{-13/2}\\right)dt=-\\dfrac{t^{-7/2}}7-\\dfrac{t^{-11/2}}{11}\\)."},{"id":"A15-0007","n":7,"sub":"15.1","yr":1978,"d":"1978-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1978","type":"sub","q":"Integrate \\(\\dfrac1{1-\\cot x}\\) or \\(\\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\sin x-\\cos x}\\).","ans":"\\(\\dfrac12\\log|\\sin x-\\cos x|+\\dfrac12x+c\\)","sol":"\\(\\sin x=\\frac12\\left[(\\sin x-\\cos x)+(\\cos x+\\sin x)\\right]\\), and \\(\\cos x+\\sin x\\) is the derivative of \\(\\sin x-\\cos x\\)."},{"id":"A15-0008","n":8,"sub":"15.1","yr":1979,"d":"1979-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1979","type":"sub","q":"Integrate \\(\\dfrac x{1+x^4}\\).","ans":"\\(\\dfrac12\\tan^{-1}(x^2)+c\\)","sol":"With \\(t=x^2\\): \\(\\dfrac12\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{dt}{1+t^2}\\)."},{"id":"A15-0009","n":9,"sub":"15.3","yr":1979,"d":"1979-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1979","type":"sub","q":"(i) Integrate \\(\\dfrac{x^2}{(a+bx)^2}\\).<br>(ii) Integrate \\(\\sin x\\sin2x\\sin3x+\\sec^2x\\cos^22x+\\sin^4x\\cos^4x\\)","ans":"(i) \\(\\dfrac1{b^3}\\left[a+bx-2a\\log|a+bx|-\\dfrac{a^2}{a+bx}\\right]+c\\)<br>(ii) \\(-\\dfrac{\\cos2x}8-\\dfrac{\\cos4x}{16}+\\dfrac{\\cos6x}{24}+\\sin2x+\\tan x-\\dfrac{253}{128}x-\\dfrac1{128}\\sin4x+\\dfrac1{1024}\\sin8x+c\\)","sol":"(i) With \\(t=a+bx\\): \\(\\dfrac1{b^3}\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{(t-a)^2}{t^2}dt=\\dfrac1{b^3}\\left[t-2a\\log|t|-\\dfrac{a^2}t\\right]\\).<br>(ii) \\(\\sin x\\sin2x\\sin3x=\\frac14(\\sin2x+\\sin4x-\\sin6x)\\); \\(\\sec^2x\\cos^22x=4\\cos^2x-4+\\sec^2x\\); \\(\\sin^4x\\cos^4x=\\frac1{16}\\sin^42x=\\frac1{128}(3-4\\cos4x+\\cos8x)\\). Integrate term by term."},{"id":"A15-0010","n":10,"sub":"15.1","yr":1979,"d":"1979-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1979","type":"sub","q":"\\(f(x)\\) is the integral of \\(\\dfrac{2\\sin x-\\sin2x}{x^3}\\), \\(x\\ne0\\) find \\(\\lim\\limits_{x\\to0}f'(x)\\).","ans":"\\(1\\)","sol":"\\(f'(x)=\\dfrac{2\\sin x(1-\\cos x)}{x^3}=2\\cdot\\dfrac{\\sin x}x\\cdot\\dfrac{1-\\cos x}{x^2}\\to2\\cdot1\\cdot\\dfrac12\\)."},{"id":"A15-0011","n":11,"sub":"15.1","yr":1980,"d":"1980-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1980","type":"sub","q":"(a) \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\sqrt{1+\\sin\\left(\\dfrac12x\\right)}\\,dx\\)<br>(b) \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{x^2}{\\sqrt{1-x}}dx\\)","ans":"(a) \\(\\pm\\left(4\\sin\\dfrac x4-4\\cos\\dfrac x4\\right)+c\\)<br>(b) \\(-2\\left[\\sqrt{1-x}-\\dfrac23(1-x)^{3/2}+\\dfrac15(1-x)^{5/2}\\right]+c\\)","sol":"(a) \\(1+\\sin\\frac x2=\\left(\\cos\\frac x4+\\sin\\frac x4\\right)^2\\). (b) With \\(t^2=1-x\\): \\(-2\\displaystyle\\int(1-t^2)^2dt\\)."},{"id":"A15-0012","n":12,"sub":"15.2","yr":1981,"d":"1981-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1981","type":"sub","q":"\\(\\displaystyle\\int(e^{\\log x}+\\sin x)\\cos x\\,dx\\)","ans":"\\(x\\sin x+\\cos x-\\dfrac{\\cos2x}4+c\\)","sol":"\\(e^{\\log x}=x\\): \\(\\displaystyle\\int x\\cos x\\,dx=x\\sin x+\\cos x\\) and \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\sin x\\cos x\\,dx=-\\dfrac{\\cos2x}4\\)."},{"id":"A15-0013","n":13,"sub":"15.2","yr":1983,"d":"1983-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1983","type":"sub","q":"\\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{(x-1)e^x}{(x+1)^3}dx\\)","ans":"\\(\\dfrac{e^x}{(x+1)^2}+c\\)","sol":"\\(\\dfrac{x-1}{(x+1)^3}=\\dfrac1{(x+1)^2}-\\dfrac2{(x+1)^3}=g+g'\\) with \\(g=\\dfrac1{(x+1)^2}\\), and \\(\\displaystyle\\int e^x(g+g')dx=e^xg\\)."},{"id":"A15-0014","n":14,"sub":"15.3","yr":1984,"d":"1984-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1984","type":"sub","q":"Evaluate \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{dx}{x^2(x^4+1)^{3/4}}\\)","ans":"\\(-\\left(1+\\dfrac1{x^4}\\right)^{1/4}+c\\)","sol":"The integrand is \\(\\dfrac1{x^5\\left(1+\\frac1{x^4}\\right)^{3/4}}\\). With \\(t=1+\\frac1{x^4}\\), \\(dt=-\\frac4{x^5}dx\\): \\(-\\dfrac14\\displaystyle\\int t^{-3/4}dt=-t^{1/4}\\)."},{"id":"A15-0015","n":15,"sub":"15.1","yr":1985,"d":"1985-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1985","type":"sub","q":"\\(\\displaystyle\\int\\sqrt{\\dfrac{1-\\sqrt x}{1+\\sqrt x}}\\,dx\\)","ans":"\\(-2\\sqrt{1-x}+\\cos^{-1}\\sqrt x+\\sqrt{x(1-x)}+c\\)","sol":"Put \\(\\sqrt x=\\cos\\theta\\): the integrand becomes \\(\\tan\\frac\\theta2\\) and \\(dx=-2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\,d\\theta\\), giving \\(-2\\displaystyle\\int(1-\\cos\\theta)\\cos\\theta\\,d\\theta=-2\\sin\\theta+\\theta+\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\)."},{"id":"A15-0016","n":16,"sub":"15.2","yr":1986,"d":"1986-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1986","type":"sub","q":"\\(I=\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{\\sin^{-1}\\sqrt x-\\cos^{-1}\\sqrt x}{\\sin^{-1}\\sqrt x+\\cos^{-1}\\sqrt x}dx\\)","ans":"\\(x-\\dfrac{4x}\\pi\\cos^{-1}\\sqrt x-\\dfrac2\\pi\\sin^{-1}\\sqrt x+\\dfrac2\\pi\\sqrt x\\sqrt{1-x}+C\\)","sol":"The denominator is \\(\\frac\\pi2\\), so the integrand is \\(1-\\dfrac4\\pi\\cos^{-1}\\sqrt x\\). By parts, \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\cos^{-1}\\sqrt x\\,dx=x\\cos^{-1}\\sqrt x+\\dfrac12\\int\\sqrt{\\dfrac x{1-x}}dx=x\\cos^{-1}\\sqrt x+\\dfrac12\\sin^{-1}\\sqrt x-\\dfrac12\\sqrt{x(1-x)}\\)."},{"id":"A15-0017","n":17,"sub":"15.3","yr":1987,"d":"1987-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1987","type":"sub","q":"Evaluate \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\left[\\dfrac{(\\cos2x)^{\\frac12}}{\\sin x}\\right]dx\\)","ans":"\\(\\sqrt2\\log\\left[\\dfrac{\\sqrt{\\cot^2x-1}+\\sqrt2\\cot x}{\\sqrt{\\cot^2x+1}}\\right]-\\log\\left[\\cot x+\\sqrt{\\cot^2x-1}\\right]+c\\)","sol":"\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{\\cos2x}}{\\sin x}=\\sqrt{\\cot^2x-1}\\). With \\(t=\\cot x\\): \\(-\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t^2-1}}{1+t^2}dt=-\\int\\dfrac{dt}{\\sqrt{t^2-1}}+2\\int\\dfrac{dt}{(1+t^2)\\sqrt{t^2-1}}\\). The first is \\(-\\log(t+\\sqrt{t^2-1})\\); the second (put \\(t=\\frac1u\\)) is \\(\\sqrt2\\log\\dfrac{\\sqrt2t+\\sqrt{t^2-1}}{\\sqrt{t^2+1}}\\)."},{"id":"A15-0018","n":18,"sub":"15.1","yr":1989,"d":"1989-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1989","type":"sub","q":"Evaluate \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\left(\\sqrt{\\tan x}+\\sqrt{\\cot x}\\right)dx\\)","ans":"\\(\\sqrt2\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{\\tan x-1}{\\sqrt{2\\tan x}}\\right)+c\\)","sol":"With \\(\\tan x=t^2\\): \\(2\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{t^2+1}{t^4+1}dt=2\\int\\dfrac{1+\\frac1{t^2}}{\\left(t-\\frac1t\\right)^2+2}dt=\\sqrt2\\tan^{-1}\\dfrac{t-\\frac1t}{\\sqrt2}\\)."},{"id":"A15-0019","n":19,"sub":"15.2","yr":1992,"d":"1992-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1992","type":"sub","q":"Find the indefinite integral \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\left(\\dfrac1{\\sqrt[3]x+\\sqrt[4]x}+\\dfrac{\\ln\\left(1+\\sqrt[6]x\\right)}{\\sqrt[3]x+\\sqrt x}\\right)dx\\)","ans":"\\(\\dfrac32x^{2/3}-\\dfrac{12}7x^{7/12}+2x^{1/2}-\\dfrac{12}5x^{5/12}+3x^{1/3}-4x^{1/4}+6x^{1/6}-12x^{1/12}+12\\ln\\left(x^{1/12}+1\\right)\\)<br>\\(+6\\left[\\left(\\dfrac{v^3}3-\\dfrac{3v^2}2+3v\\right)\\ln v-\\left(\\dfrac{v^3}9-\\dfrac{3v^2}4+3v\\right)-\\dfrac12(\\ln v)^2\\right]+c\\), where \\(v=1+x^{1/6}\\)","sol":"First part: \\(x=t^{12}\\) gives \\(12\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{t^8}{t+1}dt=12\\int\\left(t^7-t^6+t^5-t^4+t^3-t^2+t-1+\\dfrac1{t+1}\\right)dt\\). Second part: \\(x=u^6\\), \\(v=1+u\\) gives \\(6\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{(v-1)^3}v\\ln v\\,dv=6\\int\\left(v^2-3v+3-\\dfrac1v\\right)\\ln v\\,dv\\), integrated by parts. <i>(The book's printed answer has misprints in the coefficients \\(12\\) and \\(\\frac{v^3}9\\); the answer above has been checked by differentiation.)</i>"},{"id":"A15-0020","n":20,"sub":"15.2","yr":1994,"d":"1994-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1994","type":"sub","q":"Evaluate \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\cos2\\theta\\log\\left(\\dfrac{\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta}\\right)d\\theta\\)","ans":"\\(\\dfrac12\\sin2\\theta\\log\\left(\\dfrac{\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta}\\right)+\\dfrac12\\log\\cos2\\theta+C\\)","sol":"By parts: \\(\\dfrac d{d\\theta}\\log\\dfrac{\\cos\\theta+\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta}=\\dfrac2{\\cos2\\theta}\\), so the integral is \\(\\dfrac12\\sin2\\theta\\log(\\cdot)-\\displaystyle\\int\\tan2\\theta\\,d\\theta\\)."},{"id":"A15-0021","n":21,"sub":"15.3","yr":1996,"d":"1996-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1996","type":"sub","q":"Evaluate \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{(x+1)}{x(1+xe^x)^2}dx\\).","ans":"\\(\\log\\left(\\dfrac{xe^x}{1+xe^x}\\right)+\\dfrac1{1+xe^x}+C\\)","sol":"Multiply above and below by \\(e^x\\) and put \\(t=xe^x\\), \\(dt=(x+1)e^xdx\\): \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{dt}{t(1+t)^2}=\\int\\left(\\dfrac1t-\\dfrac1{1+t}-\\dfrac1{(1+t)^2}\\right)dt\\)."},{"id":"A15-0022","n":22,"sub":"15.1","yr":1997,"d":"1997-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1997","type":"sub","q":"Integrate the following \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\left(\\dfrac{1-\\sqrt x}{1+\\sqrt x}\\right)^{1/2}\\dfrac{dx}x\\)","ans":"\\(2\\cos^{-1}\\sqrt x-2\\log\\left(\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt{1-x}}{\\sqrt x}\\right)+c\\)","sol":"Put \\(\\sqrt x=\\cos\\theta\\): \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\tan\\dfrac\\theta2\\cdot\\dfrac{-2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}d\\theta=-2\\int\\dfrac{1-\\cos\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}d\\theta=2\\theta-2\\log(\\sec\\theta+\\tan\\theta)\\)."},{"id":"A15-0023","n":23,"sub":"15.3","yr":1999,"d":"1999-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1999","type":"sub","q":"Integrate \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{x^3+3x+2}{(x^2+1)^2(x+1)}dx\\)","ans":"\\(-\\dfrac12\\log|x+1|+\\dfrac14\\log(x^2+1)+\\dfrac32\\tan^{-1}x+\\dfrac x{1+x^2}+C\\)","sol":"Partial fractions: \\(\\dfrac{x^3+3x+2}{(x^2+1)^2(x+1)}=-\\dfrac1{2(x+1)}+\\dfrac{x+1}{2(x^2+1)}+\\dfrac2{(x^2+1)^2}\\), and \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{2\\,dx}{(x^2+1)^2}=\\tan^{-1}x+\\dfrac x{1+x^2}\\)."},{"id":"A15-0024","n":24,"sub":"15.2","yr":2001,"d":"2001-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 2001","type":"sub","q":"Evaluate \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{2x+2}{\\sqrt{4x^2+8x+13}}\\right)dx\\)","ans":"\\((x+1)\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{2x+2}3\\right)-\\dfrac34\\log\\left(\\dfrac{4x^2+8x+13}9\\right)+c\\)","sol":"\\(4x^2+8x+13=(2x+2)^2+9\\), so the integrand is \\(\\tan^{-1}\\dfrac{2x+2}3\\). With \\(u=\\dfrac{2x+2}3\\): \\(\\dfrac32\\displaystyle\\int\\tan^{-1}u\\,du=\\dfrac32\\left[u\\tan^{-1}u-\\dfrac12\\log(1+u^2)\\right]\\)."},{"id":"A15-0025","n":25,"sub":"15.1","yr":2002,"d":"2002-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 2002","type":"sub","q":"For any natural number \\(m\\), evaluate \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\left(x^{3m}+x^{2m}+x^m\\right)\\left(2x^{2m}+3x^m+6\\right)^{\\frac1m}dx\\), \\(x&gt;0\\).","ans":"\\(\\dfrac1{6(m+1)}\\left(2x^{3m}+3x^{2m}+6x^m\\right)^{(m+1)/m}+c\\)","sol":"Take \\(x\\) inside: \\(\\left(2x^{2m}+3x^m+6\\right)^{1/m}=\\dfrac1x\\left(2x^{3m}+3x^{2m}+6x^m\\right)^{1/m}\\). With \\(t=2x^{3m}+3x^{2m}+6x^m\\), \\(dt=6m\\left(x^{3m}+x^{2m}+x^m\\right)\\dfrac{dx}x\\): \\(\\dfrac1{6m}\\displaystyle\\int t^{1/m}dt\\)."},{"id":"A15-0026","n":26,"sub":"15.3","yr":1990,"d":"1990-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 1990","type":"fill","q":"\\(I=\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{4e^{2x}+6}{9e^{2x}-4}dx=\\) ...........","ans":"\\(-\\dfrac{3x}2+\\dfrac{35}{36}\\log\\left(9e^{2x}-4\\right)+C\\)","sol":"Write \\(4e^{2x}+6=A(9e^{2x}-4)+B\\cdot18e^{2x}\\): \\(A=-\\dfrac32\\), \\(B=\\dfrac{35}{36}\\)."},{"id":"A15-0027","n":27,"sub":"15.1","yr":2007,"d":"2007-05-20","sh":0,"src":"IIT-JEE 2007","type":"mcq","q":"Let \\(F(x)\\) be an indefinite integral of \\(\\sin^2x\\).<br><b>Statement-1 :</b> The function \\(F(x)\\) satisfies \\(F(x+\\pi)=F(x)\\) for all real \\(x\\).<br><b>Statement-2 :</b> \\(\\sin^2(x+\\pi)=\\sin^2x\\) for all real \\(x\\).","opts":["Statement-1 is True, Statement-2 is True; Statement-2 is a correct explanation of Statement-1","Statement-1 is True, Statement-2 is True; Statement-2 is NOT a correct explanation for Statement-1","Statement-1 is True, Statement-2 is False","Statement-1 is False, Statement-2 is True."],"ans":3,"sol":"\\(F(x)=\\dfrac x2-\\dfrac{\\sin2x}4+c\\), so \\(F(x+\\pi)=F(x)+\\dfrac\\pi2\\): Statement-1 is false. Statement-2 is true."}]}